{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes","id":1340731,"title":"What exactly are Sidereal themes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-10T21:58:15-07:00","id":1340731,"title":"What exactly are Sidereal themes?","content":"Solars - Just that good/ perfection/ leadership/ humanity/ golden light constructs<br /> Dragonblooded - teamwork/ the elements/ family/ bloodlines<br /> Alchemicals - transformation/ modular charms/ steampunk/ technology/ pick and refit<br /> Infernals - permanent transformations/ transhumanism/ taking from the yozis/ inhumanity/ myth and legend<br /> <br /> Urm... what are Sidereals? Solars are good at archery. They are so good, you can break their arms, throw them in the middle of a hurricane, and they can shoot a coin-sized target on the moon. Dragonblooded throw fireballs and grow arrows from the ground. Alchemicals can refit charms and with it, powers, letting them transform from deadly hulking giant that can smash down fortress walls to smooth tongued socialite that wages war with words. Infernals can do a pretty good job of imitating a god of a cult, listening to their followers' prayers and blessing them with money, talent, power, or mutations. <br /> <br /> What can Sidereals do? So far, I've seen neighbourhood relocation scheme, a part of the dodge charm tree. Another one was a stealth technique that let you move around reality unobserved and whisper subliminal messages into other peoples' ears. An awareness charm that lets you see the future impact of any decision you make. <br /> <br /> So what's their guideline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T22:50:10-07:00","id":1340737,"title":"","content":"For like charm powers? They're manipulators of fate and reality. So they have an archery charm where they whisper a message onto the bowstring, draw it back and fire it, they have a dodge charm that allows them to slip from existence as if they'd never been there in that scene at all. They also do things in an awesome roundabout way sometimes. For example they have a charm that convinces people they're lying. Like, you say something, and no matter what it is everyone who hears you is absolutely certain that you're fibbing. They're also often really elegant in a way that I find difficult to describe.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also martial arts. Solars are technically the most straightforward powerhouse martial artists, but Sidereal martial arts are crazy and esoteric. You may activate a SMA charm and suddenly the physical battle that you're having is now taking place across a series of metaphors, or you might grab hold of the strands of a person's destiny and snarl them into a pattern that nobody recognizes.<br /> <br /> <br /> From a story standpoint they're the special agents of heaven, and I think the best way I can illustrate that is by ripping off a Warhammer 40k game into and putting a text exchange between heavenly bureaus, as follows:<br /> <br /> Transcript compiled from communiques between Gloam Celestial Field Office and <b>Bureau of Heaven</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Priority Alert - Suspected Labyrinthine corruption detected.<br /> Origin - Gloam seacaves<br /> Ce<br /> Request direction for containment procedures<br /> <br /> <b>Implement sublime warding field</b><br /> <br /> Negative - Corruption spread too wide for effective warding field containment<br /> Suspected Class 4 pervasivity <br /> <br /> <b>Deploy Transmundane Brightspark</b><br /> <br /> Brightspark ineffective<br /> Personnel losses increasing<br /> Corruption spread accelerating<br /> <br /> <b>Coordinate wide area spirit courts</b><br /> <b>Unity in defense, by Mandate of Heaven</b><br /> <br /> Local agents ineffective<br /> Corruption spread CONTINUES TO ACCELERATE<br /> Corruption approaching proximity threshold for defense of Celestial Gateway<br /> <br /> <b>Executive Request Contact<br /> Petitioning Bureau of Destiny<br /> Best effort until response or relief</b><br /> <br /> Assistance urgent<br /> Population in danger<br /> Corruption breakwall OVERSPILL!<br /> <br /> <b>Bureau of Destiny response received<br /> Deploying Sidereal Exalted<br /> </b></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Basically when the world is falling apart, and all the checks and guards in place from Heaven itself are failing, and the beleaguered custodians have just about given up hope, Sidereal exalted arrive to strike fast, fix the problem with incomprehensible skills and abilities, and move on to the next one. Or alternatively when those guards and watchers are themselves corrupt, jamming up the gears of the great Bureaucracy for their own selfish gains, or just simple incompetence, the Sidereals are there in the limelight and in the shadows to set it right.<br /> <br /> Then woven through all that is the fact that they're still people themselves, with their own desires and politics and values. As a chosen of the maidens the world needs you, and there's not enough to go around, but how do you balance everything?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T03:56:20-07:00","id":1340754,"title":"","content":"One way to look at it is what they effect, generally. Solar charms manipulate their actions. Lunar charms manipulate their own bodies, Dragonblooded charms manipulate the world around them. Sidereal charms manipulate causality. <br /> <br /> A solar breaks a rock by hitting it just right. A lunar breaks a rock by making themselves strong enough to break it. A dragon blooded tells the rock to break itself. A sidereal says &quot;it is the rock's time to break&quot;, and then it breaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T04:07:47-07:00","id":1340757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1340754#post1340754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sidereal says &amp;quot;it is the rock's time to break&amp;quot;, and then it breaks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But how does that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T04:26:40-07:00","id":1340758,"title":"","content":"Maybe it turns out to have had a fault, and the sidereal's tap hits it in just the right spot so it shatters. Maybe an elephant randomly stomps through and breaks it. Maybe they ring a bell and the rock crumbles from the sound, or they fire an arrow laced with the destiny of being broken.<br /> <br /> Some kind of weird fate/plot shit happens, and the thing they want done is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T05:11:26-07:00","id":1340762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1340757#post1340757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. But how does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know a theory that if you knew the position and energy state of every single particle in existence in one instant, you could calculate all their future interactions, and thus predict the future with absolute certainty? Fate in Exalted works kinda like that - it tracks everything inside it, governs all the interactions, and predicts the future based on that. The rock's &quot;destiny&quot; is to persist until certain conditions are met - it's hit with X amount of force, it's hit in a particular point, it gets heated in forest fire and then rapidly cooled down as the nearby river overflows... basically, all the normal ways you'd expect rock to break.<br /> <br /> Now, where the Charms of other Exalted would try to break the rock by increasing the user's strength to X or beyond, or let them divine the weak point, or forcing a new break condition on the rock (&quot;the rock shall persist until my command of Earth Essence forces it to split&quot;) the Sidereal Charms would rather just change the existing conditions so the Exalt can meet them - make it so X value is lesser than the strength of their hit, or move the weak point to the exact point they're hitting, or maybe just artificially tick off the &quot;heated&quot; part of the scenario so all it takes is cooling the rock with water.<br /> <br /> In other words - Sidereals have admin-level access to reality, and can pull up people's and objects &quot;source code&quot; and make certain alterations to them to manipulate the circumstances in their favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T09:56:50-07:00","id":1340794,"title":"","content":"They are also esoteric ritualists who can gain powers by performing certain proscribed roles within the purview of their astrological specialties. Long before Solars had personas, Sidereals were the &quot;character with extra characters attached&quot; characters, though these subsidiary identities tended to be much more short-lived, and fade from attention soon after they play their part (read, when the effect and duration run out).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T13:44:13-07:00","id":1340834,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I just do not get why, when a question such as this comes up, people fall back upon vague platitudes rather than citing the actual published Charms. Especially as regards Sidereals, where the platitudes have a tendency to be the most vague and least accurate to the actual published version.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I mean, fair enough, even though Sidereals have a very strongly defined and firmly established format for their evocative powers in First Edition, the substance of that format is intricate and esoteric enough that it's hard to figure out exactly what it will look like in a form updated for Third Edition. But the existing Charm sets are still <i>something</i>, and should serve as a more solid reference point.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Now, as regards examples such as how a Sidereal breaks things, I'll admit that I had forgotten about the Charm &quot;Hungry Touch&quot;, so there is a thing that works kind of similarly to ordaining that a thing is destined to break (specifically the Sidereal could consume part of its destiny to hasten its conclusion, mechanically functioning as reducing a target number for boosting one's Strength + Athletics rating to determine what feats of destruction can be achieved).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There's also Burn Life, which just straight up spends motes to increase the rating of one's physical Attributes. So a Sidereal who wants to break something can and should simply just magically increase their Strength. There's some fluff about how doing so decreases one's lifespan a bit, but that doesn't play out in the scope of a game scene or anything.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What exactly is the Charm to </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;artificially tick off the &quot;heated&quot; part of the scenario so all it takes is cooling the rock with water&quot;? I don't know about it. A lot of Sidereal stuff actually was ultimately more direct than that. If a Sidereal wants to break a rock, they're almost definitely still hitting the rock, and one way or another need to be at least strong enough to break it. </span></span></div> <br /> <br /> So, answering a couple of question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes#post1340731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Urm... what are Sidereals?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sidereal Exalted are mystic sage bureaucrats of Heaven. They're selected from birth and lead lives auspiciously guided towards teaching them the principles of their station and their Caste up until the point they Exalt, at which point they're whisked off to Yu-Shan to be trained and take up their position. They live their lives as specialist agents of the divine bureau responsible for destiny, participating in the planning and predicting of such fates, issuing commands and coordination to the gods, and going down to Creation to personally ensure when sensitive matters unfold in the correct manner without interference.<br /> <br /> They're also politically intertwined with the circumstances of the Usurpation because of their prophecies about impending disaster having come from the ancient Solars. Hence, they function as behind the scenes advisors and enablers for the dominance of the Realm, and run counter operations against forces that threaten it, particularly the other Celestial Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can Sidereals do?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of things, it's complicated. The Five Maidens provide five overarching themes for their powers to work in, although they're still clearly tied together. The Abilities are also tied to a bunch of fictional astrological signs that provide further imagery for what their powers might do, leading to a lot of more abstract and metaphorical interpretations of them.<br /> <br /> I can think of... three broad summaries of how Sidereal Charms tend to function. The first are fairly straightforward things that are given some fluff to make some destiny interaction the basis of how they function, with limited practical output. There are times when some of the stronger effects of such are tied to some limited circumstance or resource expenditure.<br /> <br /> A lot of their powers involve interacting with or manipulating things in odd ways. Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme is an example, being able to physically drag an area around to place it in a new place. There are powers to kind of absorb and reapply some things, and they can inflict strange transformations. Also a few powers that involve kind of... slipping behind the scenes to get from point a to point b, to evade notice or to have unusual angles for manipulating things.<br /> <br /> (There are some powers that involve generating an effect through what is basically casting a spell that I'd put as a crossover between the two)<br /> <br /> And there's the stuff to do with seeing or affecting the future. Largely things to let Sidereals see the future, although never in a direct manner; you get things like seeing a future from the perspective of a world where it already happened, or being limited to assessing options that will further a stated goal. They have at least one power based on weaponizing revealing another person's future to them, and a few odder things such as striking a person and giving them an option between taking the severe damage that it can inflict or allowing themselves to be cursed with some harmful random happenstance coming upon them later on.<br /> <br /> They're not supposed to be able to come up with their own Charms, so the actions of Sidereals are very strongly guided by the limits of what their Charms can do, and there set is supposed to be very tightly designed to have a number of powers that combine or sequence well to achieve results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T14:09:12-07:00","id":1340839,"title":"","content":"In terms of Storytelling, Sidereals can be about :<br /> <br /> -Having your life decided for you and being expected to fall in line. Doing the same to others.<br /> <br /> -Being tasked with keeping a failing system running despite being vastly understaffed and poorly managed. Sticking to one's duty even when the outcome is likely eventual failure.<br /> <br /> -Having to play by the rules or facing drastic consequences. Being torn when doing the right thing would require you to commit sacrilege.<br /> <br /> -Knowing much about your own future and that of those close to you, and how that impacts the decisions you make.<br /> <br /> -Holding the reins of history yet having no one who remembers <b>you</b>.<br /> <br /> -Being in it for the long, long game. Planning the rise and fall of entire empires in advance, and steeling your heart when you orchestrate disasters which you know are necessary for the world's survival and stability.<br /> <br /> -Preserving your humanity even though you must play with mortal lives and decide people's fates for them to achieve your aims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 10-11-2019, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T14:46:41-07:00","id":1340846,"title":"","content":"Accelerator, the themes of the Sidereals are Fate, Destiny and foresight.<br /> <br /> Unless you want to explore what those words mean to you - and unless you take seriously at least for the game's cosmology that they do have coherent meanings - you probably won't be able to get far with what the Sidereals are about! In pith, to be a Sidereal is to be person who gets power from Fate, Destiny and foresight, but is also uniquely bound by the strictures of that power and to face unique choices as a consequence of foresight.<br /> <br /> Further than that, they represent the idea of destiny and Fate as a subtle, but decisive hidden force, ordered by mysterious patterns. To that end their powers are intended to be subtle, but decisive and ordered in partially opaque structures ordered by symbolism and subtext, and which, when experienced, have unexpected synergies! To that end the experience of playing a Sidereal is to play a person who is a hidden force, much as Fate itself is!<br /> <br /> These themes are structured within the five houses of Journeys, Battles, Secrets, Endings and Serenity, each of which is rich in mythic narrative and potential for human connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T20:32:12-07:00","id":1341044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes#post1340731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can Sidereals do? So far, I've seen neighbourhood relocation scheme, a part of the dodge charm tree. Another one was a stealth technique that let you move around reality unobserved and whisper subliminal messages into other peoples' ears. An awareness charm that lets you see the future impact of any decision you make.<br /> <br /> So what's their guideline?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that I totally understand the question, but a lot of people have answered according to their interpretations. To me, Sidereals are another angle of Exalted's deconstruction of power fantasy, in which every Exalt-type understands and expresses power differently. Sidereals are a personification of <i>exploitation</i> and <i>understanding</i>. They exploit influence, people, tools, wisdom, knowledge, coincidence, human nature, bureaucracy, physics, wordplay, and even themselves (see the Charm &quot;Burn Life&quot;). They're legendary martial arts masters because they can understand the secret power of martial arts like nobody else can. They make effective viziers and operatives because they see the world like nobody else does, and they're untrustworthy for the same reason. They're expected to use any tool at their disposal, including each other, because they often see little other choice.<br /> <br /> Edit: The 1st Edition Athletics tree really says it all. They achieve basic Exalted Athletics competence by cheating their lifespan, timing, gravity, and the fundamental mechanics of the human body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 10-12-2019, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T09:10:23-07:00","id":1341096,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are system administrators with special system privileges, permissions, and approved cheat codes and exploits, and limited item-spawning and code-manipulation abilities.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are agents of Fate and ambassadors of heaven, whose power derives from the authority of others. When they flash their badges, you must submit to the authority invested in them, or suffer the weapons granted to them.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re like the Agents of the Matrix, whereas Getimians are like the humans who plug back into the system and break the code to their liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T10:23:42-07:00","id":1341105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341044#post1341044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that I totally understand the question, but a lot of people have answered according to their interpretations. To me, Sidereals are another angle of Exalted's deconstruction of power fantasy, in which every Exalt-type understands and expresses power differently. Sidereals are a personification of <i>exploitation</i> and <i>understanding</i>. They exploit influence, people, tools, wisdom, knowledge, coincidence, human nature, bureaucracy, physics, wordplay, and even themselves (see the Charm &quot;Burn Life&quot;). They're legendary martial arts masters because they can understand the secret power of martial arts like nobody else can. They make effective viziers and operatives because they see the world like nobody else does, and they're untrustworthy for the same reason. They're expected to use any tool at their disposal, including each other, because they often see little other choice.<br /> <br /> Edit: The 1st Edition Athletics tree really says it all. They achieve basic Exalted Athletics competence by cheating their lifespan, timing, gravity, and the fundamental mechanics of the human body.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e Sidereal Athletics? <a href=\"https://youtu.be/aeiSVFrl_sI?t=247\" target=\"_blank\">Time for Hungry Touch.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T08:49:45-07:00","id":1341265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341096#post1341096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re like the Agents of the Matrix, whereas Getimians are like the humans who plug back into the system and break the code to their liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>More accurately Getimians are humans who've been migrated from a different system and brought some of its rules with them.<br /> <br /> Morke basically felt that introducing a dedicated red pill (Jesus, there's a term that's <b>not</b> aged well) exalt type as a Sidereal foil would mostly serve to cast them as agents of stagnation and vilify them in their own stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T07:44:04-07:00","id":1341438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341265#post1341265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as a Sidereal foil would mostly serve to cast them as agents of stagnation and vilify them in their own stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's silly. Fighting to defend a status quo can be made into one of the most heroic things in the world; just look at the Alchemical Exalted.<br /> <br /> If the Sidereal Exalted cannot feel heroic while serving Heaven, that's a statement about Heaven rather than them.<br /> <br /> Though if memory serves, their Sutras show a disturbing malice towards children.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jesus, there's a term that's <b>not</b> aged well </div> </div> </div>Not as poorly as ABC's coverage of the &quot;Turkish bombardment of the Kurds&quot;, which turned out to be altered footage of an American artillery show in Kentucky.<br /> <br /> Or the footage of &quot;corpses&quot; under sheets that can't lay still for two minutes, and the &quot;dead&quot; baby that starts blinking in his mother's arms.<br /> <br /> The Matrix is breaking down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 10-15-2019, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T11:25:35-07:00","id":1341479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341438#post1341438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just look at the Alchemical Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Alchemical Exalted probably benefit a lot from not having a whole new group of Exalted set against them from a perspective that fighting in defence of the Octet is terrible and dull.<br /> <br /> Is your Matrix analogy merely a reference to illustrate, or do you think the Sidereal Exalted should be a one-to-one picture of the Agents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T13:19:42-07:00","id":1341500,"title":"","content":"Meta-comment: For Lioness to reveal that John was sensitive to precisely that issue really makes me want to see how his brief for them evolves (and wish that we had already seen it, but that's kind of a plaintive yet not constructive comment !).<br /> <br /> (Add: The Sidereals have received better than us seeing them in a disenchanted technological metaphor that stresses borrowed power, and robs them of their mythic resonance. We have their presentations in the books. It'd be kind of nice to see for us to eventually if what JM's vision of the Getimians were in a way which feels hewn out of magic, myth and poetry. Which we don't really have in a well articulated, fleshed out form.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T18:04:56-07:00","id":1341532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341479#post1341479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Alchemical Exalted probably benefit a lot from not having a whole new group of Exalted set against them</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> from a perspective that fighting in defence of the Octet is terrible and dull.<br /> <br /> Is your Matrix analogy merely a reference to illustrate, or do you think the Sidereal Exalted should be a one-to-one picture of the Agents? </div> </div> </div>Merely a reference, and certainly not a moral judgment.<br /> <br /> On that note:<br /> <br /> I went back to look at the Sidereal Scriptures, and it seems that only two of them are hostile to children. They just stuck out most in my memory since they were so horrible.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Scripture of the Drowning Maiden features a drowning maiden whose every attempt to breathe kills &quot;a human child&quot;. If her breathing killed anyone regardless of age or character, it could be taken as a statement of <i>Exalted's</i> universe's indifference. It's not a statement about her morality because there's no clue whether she's doing this intentionally or specifically targeting children for her own gain.<br /> <br /> What's additionally confusing is the thesis that &quot;Survival is acceptance&quot;. Who is supposed to be accepting anything? Is she accepting that she must kill to survive, or must the children accept that they must die? The scripture doesn't present the idea that killing others is a thing she rejected and had to learn to accept, since the bit about killing children only comes up in the penultimate line.<br /> <br /> The final confusing bit is that this is the scripture for Brawl, which has no Charm for survival by putting your tribulation on someone else. That's Someone Else's Destiny, a Charm under Resistance, whose scripture involves nothing about killing others for survival.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Scripture of the Maiden on the Shelf is the other one, and it belongs to the Melee Ability.<br /> <br /> The scripture is of a doll that watches the world from a shelf, until it disappears along with a child's severed head. Most of the poem is about what the doll looks like and that it does nothing but watch, so I'm not sure how it leads to a thesis that &quot;Survival is control&quot;, or what that has to do with the Melee Ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dishonorable mention goes to the Scripture of the Expectant Maiden, for Martial Arts, where the maiden wishes to kill &quot;the boy&quot; who put her &quot;there&quot;, but at least in that case it's clearly a case of specific revenge, with the boy representing anything or anyone.<br /> <br /> It's tempting to draw a connection with the Scripture of the Maiden on the Shelf, but it would seem to be the only time two different scriptures are linked, so it's a dubious theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T18:30:19-07:00","id":1341542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341532#post1341532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fair point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Merely a reference, and certainly not a moral judgment.<br /> <br /> On that note:<br /> <br /> I went back to look at the Sidereal Scriptures, and it seems that only two of them are hostile to children. They just stuck out most in my memory since they were so horrible.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Scripture of the Drowning Maiden features a drowning maiden whose every attempt to breathe kills &quot;a human child&quot;. If her breathing killed anyone regardless of age or character, it could be taken as a statement of <i>Exalted's</i> universe's indifference. It's not a statement about her morality because there's no clue whether she's doing this intentionally or specifically targeting children for her own gain.<br /> <br /> What's additionally confusing is the thesis that &quot;Survival is acceptance&quot;. Who is supposed to be accepting anything? Is she accepting that she must kill to survive, or must the children accept that they must die? The scripture doesn't present the idea that killing others is a thing she rejected and had to learn to accept, since the bit about killing children only comes up in the penultimate line.<br /> <br /> The final confusing bit is that this is the scripture for Brawl, which has no Charm for survival by putting your tribulation on someone else. That's Someone Else's Destiny, a Charm under Resistance, whose scripture involves nothing about killing others for survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Gauntlet for you - bad and worse. The line in particular regarding drowning children seems to be a reflection of Crimson Palm Counterstrike, and if you zoom out a bit, everyone is someone's child, so it seems to be suggesting that any use of it in combat is going to result in an unpleasant exchange. The last line refers to the Prayer Strip Charm, which can enable survival if someone else accepts it over far worse damage to themself, given the stated mechanics of the Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Scripture of the Maiden on the Shelf is the other one, and it belongs to the Melee Ability.<br /> <br /> The scripture is of a doll that watches the world from a shelf, until it disappears along with a child's severed head. Most of the poem is about what the doll looks like and that it does nothing but watch, so I'm not sure how it leads to a thesis that &quot;Survival is control&quot;, or what that has to do with the Melee Ability. </div> </div> </div>The archetypal character of the College of the Spear is a soldier. Consider how one sees training of recruits, or their life journey - frequently, they'll start not long after they've become recognized adults, which is still a fairly young age. A fair number of locations in Creation probably don't even wait for that recognition. It could be sort of like The Lovers, in that regard, in that it's a really shitty take that nonetheless represents how the Maidens see the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dishonorable mention goes to the Scripture of the Expectant Maiden, for Martial Arts, where the maiden wishes to kill &quot;the boy&quot; who put her &quot;there&quot;, but at least in that case it's clearly a case of specific revenge, with the boy representing anything or anyone.<br /> <br /> It's tempting to draw a connection with the Scripture of the Maiden on the Shelf, but it would seem to be the only time two different scriptures are linked, so it's a dubious theory. </div> </div> </div>The Maiden on the Shelf doesn't specify a boy, though. It only mentions a child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T19:37:51-07:00","id":1341558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341532#post1341532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scripture of the Drowning Maiden features a drowning maiden whose every attempt to breathe kills &quot;a human child&quot;. If her breathing killed anyone regardless of age or character, it could be taken as a statement of <i>Exalted's</i> universe's indifference. It's not a statement about her morality because there's no clue whether she's doing this intentionally or specifically targeting children for her own gain.<br /> <br /> What's additionally confusing is the thesis that &quot;Survival is acceptance&quot;. Who is supposed to be accepting anything? Is she accepting that she must kill to survive, or must the children accept that they must die? The scripture doesn't present the idea that killing others is a thing she rejected and had to learn to accept, since the bit about killing children only comes up in the penultimate line.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Maiden is powerless. She's trapped in a blinding, freezing descent without purchase or mobility. There's not even escape through death, and it instead puts that loss on others to preserve her life. In such a circumstance as that, there is no recourse but acceptance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The final confusing bit is that this is the scripture for Brawl, which has no Charm for survival by putting your tribulation on someone else. That's Someone Else's Destiny, a Charm under Resistance, whose scripture involves nothing about killing others for survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at the fluff and mechanics of the Charms, the Sidereal Brawler is not the one who must accept; the Sidereal Brawler is the inevitability that must <i>be</i> accepted.<br /> <br /> Looking at it now, I strongly suspect that the associations there arise from the common idiom use of the term &quot;gauntlet&quot; to refer to a circumstance of suffering and using it as the literal basis for fist fighting.<br /> <br /> I guess that's another thing to see in how Sidereals express their themes, making those metaphorical connotations the logic behind their Abilities. Most parts of Sidereal Brawl before Easily-Accepted Proposition Stance are visually straightforward as punching people, but it's punching that can hardly be escape or undermined as an expression of the thesis of that constellation and scripture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scripture of the Maiden on the Shelf is the other one, and it belongs to the Melee Ability.<br /> <br /> The scripture is of a doll that watches the world from a shelf, until it disappears along with a child's severed head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, within the scope of poetry and archetype, a doll isn't going to be in the possession of an adult. I think it being a child is incidental, the point is that when the doll elects to leave, it takes the head of its owner with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the poem is about what the doll looks like</div> </div> </div> </div>More than just that; it's a focused description on the form of the eyes and an expression that is fixed and artificial. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">that it does nothing but watch, so I'm not sure how it leads to a thesis that &quot;Survival is control&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The doll is patient in the extreme, totally aware while wasting nothing in extraneous movement or feeling, until the ordained moment comes and it acts with severity and no hesitation. It possesses both self-control and control over its circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">or what that has to do with the Melee Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>The particular Sidereal interpretation of the Melee Ability seems to be focused on observation and precision, which I think often comes up in real life fencing philosophies anyway. It makes me think a lot about the outlook and fighting style of the character of Ashina Isshin from Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice, a man whose very name means &quot;single-mindedness&quot; and &quot;no hesitation&quot;.<br /> <br /> I propose that the Spear, the sign of discipline and precision, is represented by a doll rather than a Maiden because a doll would appear to be a static and immobile thing, unburdened by flesh or needs or morality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dishonorable mention goes to the Scripture of the Expectant Maiden, for Martial Arts, where the maiden wishes to kill &quot;the boy&quot; who put her &quot;there&quot;, but at least in that case it's clearly a case of specific revenge, with the boy representing anything or anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contextually, it also reads to me as not using the term &quot;boy&quot; to refer to a literal child, and more in the colloquial manner of referring to an adult of some intimacy.<br /> <br /> Besides, if there's anything to be disturbed by in the Scripture of the Expectant Maiden, I would say that it's not in plotting the death of somebody, child or otherwise, but in representing the perspective of somebody who keeps putting fulfilment off to the future and unwilling to accept that it's never coming, before their life ends and their hopes amounted to nothing. That's certainly the part that's touching me right now.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Accelerator, this is the thing about the power of Sidereals (and a bit of what Dex Davican was saying earlier); what power they have over fate isn't so much in &quot;we can just make whatever happen as we please&quot; so much as it is being the enforcers of &quot;you cannot escape your destiny, you can only choose how to meet it&quot;. They know the underlying principles of Destiny and embody them through their capabilities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T20:36:55-07:00","id":1342005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341532#post1341532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scripture of the Drowning Maiden features a drowning maiden whose every attempt to breathe kills &quot;a human child&quot;. If her breathing killed anyone regardless of age or character, it could be taken as a statement of <i>Exalted's</i> universe's indifference. It's not a statement about her morality because there's no clue whether she's doing this intentionally or specifically targeting children for her own gain.<br /> <br /> What's additionally confusing is the thesis that &quot;Survival is acceptance&quot;. Who is supposed to be accepting anything? Is she accepting that she must kill to survive, or must the children accept that they must die? The scripture doesn't present the idea that killing others is a thing she rejected and had to learn to accept, since the bit about killing children only comes up in the penultimate line.</div> </div> </div> </div> I personally read it as her own acceptance that her life comes at the cost of other lives. I'd say that the sutra raises the question of whether there's a moral difference between killing to survive and surviving at the cost of someone else's life. Easily Accepted Proposition Stance (which, in retrospect, is Charmspeak for &quot;an offer you can't refuse&quot;) puts that moral choice on the Sidereal's most powerful opponent. Will that person choose survival by accepting the Sidereal's dictum, or reject an unjust fate at the cost of their own life (or at least their health).<br /> <br /> Note that the most effective way to use this as a killing weapon is to declare a destiny that your opponent will find too abhorrent to accept, a cost they won't pay to survive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Scripture of the Maiden on the Shelf is the other one, and it belongs to the Melee Ability.<br /> <br /> The scripture is of a doll that watches the world from a shelf, until it disappears along with a child's severed head. Most of the poem is about what the doll looks like and that it does nothing but watch, so I'm not sure how it leads to a thesis that &quot;Survival is control&quot;, or what that has to do with the Melee Ability. </div> </div> </div> I read this sutra as an examination of the very Sidereal philosophy that &quot;apparently-harmless or even beloved observer&quot; is a role from which a canny person can exert significant control. It merely requires a willingness to discard love and the appearance of agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T12:37:34-07:00","id":1342149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341542#post1341542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the Gauntlet for you - bad and worse. The line in particular regarding drowning children seems to be a reflection of Crimson Palm Counterstrike, and if you zoom out a bit, everyone is someone's child, so it seems to be suggesting that any use of it in combat is going to result in an unpleasant exchange.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the target of Crimson Palm Counterstrike is an opponent trying to do a Sidereal harm, and the children in the scripture have nothing to do with the Maiden's tribulation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Maiden on the Shelf doesn't specify a boy, though. It only mentions a child. </div> </div> </div>The Expectant Maiden does specify a boy, though. I said that &quot;a boy&quot; can be &quot;a child&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T14:56:31-07:00","id":1342191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341438#post1341438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's silly.</div> </div> </div> </div> Remember we're not talking about if Sidereal games can have themes of questioning if Yu-Shan and the greater design of fate are worth fighting for, we're talking about the introduction of a hypothetical new exalt type to bring them to the forefront.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 10-18-2019, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T10:55:44-07:00","id":1342373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1342149#post1342149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the target of Crimson Palm Counterstrike is an opponent trying to do a Sidereal harm, and the children in the scripture have nothing to do with the Maiden's tribulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that &quot;Children&quot; in this context could refer to &quot;Children of Earth&quot; or a similar concept, i.e. mortals. Lots of sobriquets also refer to character types of presumably adult characters as &quot;Children of ...&quot; or the like, so it doesn't need to refer to actual juveniles. Also, most of these people have nothing to do with a Sidereal's missions and life, but she still crosses in-between them nonetheless, and that causes anything from complications to mortality along her line of work preserving destiny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Expectant Maiden does specify a boy, though. I said that &quot;a boy&quot; can be &quot;a child&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Any references to a state of youth in an Endings scripture - as a rule, always about transitions and changes of state - are probably fleeting and in the past. This is setting aside other colloquial uses of the word &quot;boy&quot;, like &quot;old boy&quot; of a school, referring to a graduate and hence probably not a child, or an address of confrontation toward a man, potentially one younger and less experienced, or abhorrent &quot;boys will be boys&quot;. It tends to flavor the scripture with a tone of familiarity with the individual responsible for the focus character's predicament, rather than referring to a juvenile, male-gendered individual. Literal readings seem to be the last thing in mind for most Sidereal scriptures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T16:44:16-07:00","id":1342435,"title":"","content":"I think that Sidereal scriptures of all things aren't exactly about literal readings. The Maiden in Dust is not about constantly reminding people that you're going to die, for instance.<br /> <br /> I read talk about getting back at &quot;that boy&quot;, and it just makes me think about how Darla referred to Angel. That might just be because I've been rewatching that show recently.<br /> <br /> I mean, look at that line in context of a person talking about all of the fulfillment that they're surely going to have tomorrow. Does revenge on a child really fit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T05:35:01-07:00","id":1343562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1341500#post1341500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meta-comment: For Lioness to reveal that John was sensitive to precisely that issue really makes me want to see how his brief for them evolves (and wish that we had already seen it, but that's kind of a plaintive yet not constructive comment !)</div> </div> </div> </div>He also had an interesting conversation with a friend of mine where he explained how some of the existing potential foils have been squandered by the presentation of previous editions.<br /> <br /> Most notably agreeing that the Lotus Massacre had really not endeared veteran Sidereal players to the idea of being the cold war CIA/MI6 to the Green Sun Prince's KGB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T07:51:32-07:00","id":1343582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1342435#post1342435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Sidereal scriptures of all things aren't exactly about literal readings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm complaining about the ones that don't seem to fit metaphorical themes of what the Charms do.<br /> <br /> Did you really think I was demanding literal interpretations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T08:06:17-07:00","id":1343587,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are the favored servants/pawns/children/slaves of a set of goddesses who claim to be more or less omniscient and claim to be working for the Greater Good without every revealing what that Greater Good is, and who may or may not be sub-sapient machines carrying out their programming without any real goals/soulless chessmasters who move everyone and everything about as puppets on a stage in the service of goals that only they can see and only they care about.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are the Chosen of Destiny, noble defenders of the causality who have to make hard choices in the service of what they believe is the best future, who are reassured by the Maidens that, yes, indeed, it is for a good future and even if it wasn't its still better than every other alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T09:46:25-07:00","id":1343604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343582#post1343582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you really think I was demanding literal interpretations?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the line you've quoted, I was not taking to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T10:42:15-07:00","id":1343609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1342373#post1342373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that &quot;Children&quot; in this context could refer to &quot;Children of Earth&quot; or a similar concept, i.e. mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. If I didn't concede that earlier, I'll concede that point now.<br /> <br /> But the poem could be talking about kittens or apples for all I care, because that's not the point I was making <i>there</i>.<br /> <br /> The Drowning Maiden is struggling against her descent, the water, the dark, the cold... The children have nothing to do with any of that, so if her circumstances represent the opponents that the Brawler is struggling against to survive, then the children can't represent some of those opponents. They would more logically represent bystanders.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343604#post1343604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the line you've quoted, I was not taking to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 10-25-2019, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T12:22:50-07:00","id":1343629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343609#post1343609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. If I didn't concede that earlier, I'll concede that point now.<br /> <br /> But the poem could be talking about kittens or apples for all I care, because that's not the point I was making <i>there</i>.<br /> <br /> The Drowning Maiden is struggling against her descent, the water, the dark, the cold... The children have nothing to do with any of that, so if her circumstances represent the opponents that the Brawler is struggling against to survive, then the children can't represent some of those opponents. They would more logically represent bystanders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crowds of folk who are not skilled in combat tend to be treated as environments, and environments tend to take collateral damage, sometimes in very extreme fashion, when the Exalted take to the field. Anyone who doesn't clear out quickly enough at the earliest signs of trouble, and sometimes even those who do, are going to suffer for it, possibly at the hands of the one that didn't start or want it but who isn't going to sit back and wait to die. This is the use of unrestrained force in a nutshell; a vast sea that washes over everything and spares very few, if any, from its touch. If this seems callous or horrible... the description of the constellation is pretty much in line with that, since it seems to be all about the cliche of &quot;hard men making hard decisions&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T12:38:44-07:00","id":1343632,"title":"","content":"Then they should write a less clunky metaphor, not something that evokes an overly arcane butterfly effect. Its like telling kids if they don't eat their vegetables then someone overseas will die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T12:58:45-07:00","id":1343637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343609#post1343609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> if her circumstances represent the opponents that the Brawler is struggling against to survive</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sidereal is not the one drowning, they are the water.<br /> <br /> Sidereal Brawl is about taking the proverbial gauntlet, the metaphor for grueling challenges and struggles, and wrapping it around their clenched fist.<br /> <br /> The thing about children is just a poetic image for lacking any method of relief or escape. It's not even an analogy for something else, just a vivid, punchy, memorable way of making the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T12:59:52-07:00","id":1343638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343632#post1343632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its like telling kids if they don't eat their vegetables then someone overseas will die.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised if that's ever happened in Nobilis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T08:49:27-07:00","id":1343782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343632#post1343632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then they should write a less clunky metaphor, not something that evokes an overly arcane butterfly effect. Its like telling kids if they don't eat their vegetables then someone overseas will die.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a butterfly effect, but a direct and observable consequence. You scrap in a population center, and people get tossed aside like rag dolls. Get in a fight around cropland, and there goes the harvest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T10:24:49-07:00","id":1343797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343782#post1343782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a butterfly effect, but a direct and observable consequence. You scrap in a population center, and people get tossed aside like rag dolls. Get in a fight around cropland, and there goes the harvest.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how does that translate from &quot;with every breath she takes while trying to stop drowing, this person kills X amount of children&quot;? Its not an immediate consequence of &quot;stop drowning&quot;, its something so far down the line of causality that it sounds like a contrivance, as opposed to using a more direct metaphor. If you're talking about combat use a combat imagery, not this obscure bullshit you can spin to blame a dude taking a swim for mass murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T10:38:38-07:00","id":1343798,"title":"","content":"That's kinda the point of Sids. They're not direct. Their sutras aren't literal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T10:45:03-07:00","id":1343803,"title":"","content":"Of course, the implication is they will do horrific shit based on chains of reasoning so contrived that one wonders whether or not they're really justified. Which isn't very healthy for the gameline. If the Sidereals say &quot;we have to raze this kingdom to prevent the second Contagion&quot; its kind of hard to take their word for it when they've been proven to be disastrously fallible in the past. Obligate reasoning like a person with a mental illness shouldn't be built into a gameline, but its been part of Sid themes before.<br /> <br /> The Maidens are supposed to support the continuation of Creation, but the way they do so in other editions is so contrived that it makes them suspect. Mars supported the Usurpation because she knew it would cause more warfare in Creation, how does that translate to &quot;protect Creation&quot;? What's the chain of causality here? Something so obscure that only the Maidens can see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 10-26-2019, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T10:55:47-07:00","id":1343808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343803#post1343803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mars supported the Usurpation</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a source on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T10:57:11-07:00","id":1343809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343808#post1343808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a source on that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2e Sids Splat, Bureau of Battles writeup I think. Its more speculation on the part of her servitors, but its emblematic of the idea that the Maidens are more corrupt than they appear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 10-26-2019, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T11:07:13-07:00","id":1343812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343809#post1343809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 2e Sids Splat, Bureau of Battles writeup I think</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That's not what that says. It says some people <i>wonder</i> if she <i>allowed</i> it to happen to cause more war, and others speculate if she was curious to see if the Deebs could do it. But that's not what her actual motivation was: it's speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T11:13:31-07:00","id":1343815,"title":"","content":"It still introduces the possibility that the Maidens aren't putting Creation's best interests first.<br /> <br /> Glories of the Most High:<br /> <br /> [QUOTE]The Maidens set out on the perilous journey through time to meet Luna on Creation\u2019s first night, knowing they would be bound to act (mostly) impartially for the benefit of Creation but <b>believing they could steer the course of events in their favor anyway[</b>/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Working for any intelligence agency has a deal of ethical ambiguity about it, but the Bureau of Destiny has traditionally been closer to an authoritarian/corrupt secret police than one where rule of law and human rights are a genuine concern.<br /> <br /> On Jupiter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some of Jupiter\u2019s underlings claim that she supported the Usurpation because she knew that in its aftermath, Creation would be ruled by conspirators and liars, all of whom implicitly prayed to her with every evasion and falsehood that crossed their lips </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her Chosen suspect she occasionally abuses her position by ordering the murder of some mortal savant on the verge of returning lost lore of the First Age to widespread circulation </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 10-26-2019, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T11:45:51-07:00","id":1343824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343782#post1343782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You scrap in a population center, and people get tossed aside like rag dolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Exalted has acquired an odd standard of how much collateral damage is necessary or to be expected from fights. People often talk about levels of destruction that don't quite track logically.<br /> <br /> Fists are not bullets, and bystanders can be safe enough of they move a few metres away.<br /> <br /> I think you're interpreting the line about breath incorrectly, by the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343797#post1343797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're talking about combat use a combat imagery, not this obscure bullshit you can spin to blame a dude taking a swim for mass murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though this is a perspective informed by lack of familiarity with English language poetry.<br /> <br /> Mind, I think poetry in many languages also has a tendency for more abstract and metaphorical imagery.<br /> <br /> In any case, the constellation under Battles that Sidereal Brawl powers is not about combat. It's about the role of the proverbial dice determining where the cannon shell lands, and who will be helplessly blasted to smithereens by it. The Sidereal in this case being the shell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343803#post1343803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which isn't very healthy for the gameline. </div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals arguably have a more consistent focus on doing things intended to be for the benefit of people at large than the Scarlet Dynasty does, and we've gotten two books concerned with how to play them with more sophistication than &quot;tear the whole system down and replace it with liberal democracy&quot;.<br /> <br /> I suppose that another way to answer the question of Accelerator is that one of the themes of Sidereals is having responsibility for the well being of a universe that, in the grand tradition of pulp fantasy, is unsympathetic to human life (although not strictly brutal to it either), with the ruthless calculation of a Chinese mandarin. It's not for everybody, but the priority is on making it compelling by presenting strongly motivated characters with elaborate methods and world views more than it is on creating good people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T13:33:16-07:00","id":1343851,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been awhile since I read it, but I always thought that the Scripture of the Expectant Maiden was referring to her planning to murder her baby daddy, who might then be referred to by the term \u201cboy\u201d in a use that was both familiar and insulting, but would certainly not be a child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T15:03:28-07:00","id":1343868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343824#post1343824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Exalted has acquired an odd standard of how much collateral damage is necessary or to be expected from fights. People often talk about levels of destruction that don't quite track logically.<br /> <br /> Fists are not bullets, and bystanders can be safe enough of they move a few metres away.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Brawl is also about improvised weaponry. The acquisition and use of improvised weaponry tends, by genre, to involve a fair bit of collateral damage, even before we circle back to fists often being more destructive than bullets in Exalted, such as where knockback is involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T15:27:53-07:00","id":1343872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343868#post1343868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The acquisition and use of improvised weaponry tends, by genre, to involve a fair bit of collateral damage</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be, but not really of the kind that resembles what you were describing with people being flung about.<br /> <br /> I mean sure, one can portray a Solar or Sidereal or whatever as picking up a bar stool to use as a weapon while somebody is already sitting on it, which might even be a source of injury rather than physical comedy, but even that would have to be something done very deliberately rather than an emergent consequence of things getting out of hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">we circle back to fists often being more destructive than bullets in Exalted, such as where knockback is involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... no. Even accounting for knockback, there just isn't nearly the range, lack of discernment or immediacy of being struck by a stray bullet.<br /> <br /> But even that is besides the point. I propose that as a player and a Storyteller, one needs to very much go out of their way to make other people get caught in the effects of attacks.<br /> <br /> As genre emulation goes, I'm fine with looking to something like the inn fight in Crouching Tiger where the furnishings get destroyed, but I think the subject of stray attacks catching civilians is fraught enough to be carefully considered, and often avoided. At least not when employing a weapon like Stormcaller where managing such danger is very much part of the point.<br /> <br /> But this is all tangential, since I don't view it as the point of the line in the scripture, which I think is more concerned with embodying no win scenarios that a target has to reconcile themselves with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T16:20:49-07:00","id":1343881,"title":"","content":"To go back to something for a moment:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1340731-what-exactly-are-sidereal-themes?p=1343815#post1343815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still introduces the possibility that the Maidens aren't putting Creation's best interests first.<br /> <br /> Glories of the Most High:</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the wider context presented in that book, such as the write-ups of the individual Maidens, as well as familiarity with other sentiments of the writer, I feel confident in suggesting that the meaning of the line you've quoted was supposed to be that the Maidens are capable of having personal passions that they can value over their innate function of robotically administering reality. While also praying it in terms of them being able to cannily rig the game so that they can fulfill both impulses at once.<br /> <br /> Look at the Glories entries for Mercury or Venus and tell me if you think they were supposed to be read as meaning that their agendas were sinister.*<br /> <br /> Sure, that was a departure from how Manual Sidereals portrayed them, but there are many respects in which that book is not held in high regard in the community. Among those is that it's kind of a nadir of Second Edition leaning towards presenting Creation in the most cynical terms possible, where everything is kind of grinding and miserable. I understand if it casts Sidereal Exalted in a bad light, but it was a time that wore itself out.<br /> <br /> The important thing is that it's not something intrinsic to Sidereals to the point where they need to be written like that again, and we can see from the current writing that they probably won't be. Heck, they may well end up a bit more positive and affirming than I would speculate or suggest about them.<br /> <br /> * It ultimately might not exactly be sensible, but that's kind of the byline with major characters of Exalted. And in cases where they show up as characters, the tension between an innate metaphysical duty and a wish to take risks to make things more appealing to them can be endearing and has a lot of dramatic potential to grapple with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 10-26-2019, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}